('physics-temperature-scales-01','physics','thermodynamics','Thermal properties','Temperature scales','A temperature of 27 °C is approximately:','["246 K","273 K","300 K","327 K"]',2,'Kelvin temperature is Celsius temperature plus 273.15, so 27 °C≈300 K.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-thermal-expansion-01','physics','thermodynamics','Thermal properties','Thermal expansion','For a rod of initial length L with linear expansion coefficient α, a small temperature rise ΔT produces length change:','["αLΔT","αL/ΔT","LΔT/α","αΔT/L"]',0,'Linear thermal expansion is ΔL=αLΔT.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-calorimetry-01','physics','thermodynamics','Thermal properties','Calorimetry','Ignoring phase change, heat required to raise mass m through ΔT is:','["mc/ΔT","mΔT/c","mcΔT","cΔT/m"]',2,'By definition of specific heat capacity, Q=mcΔT.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-heat-transfer-01','physics','thermodynamics','Thermal properties','Heat transfer','Which mode of heat transfer can occur through vacuum?','["conduction only","convection only","radiation","conduction and convection"]',2,'Electromagnetic thermal radiation does not require a material medium.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-newton-cooling-01','physics','thermodynamics','Thermal properties','Newton law of cooling','For small temperature differences, Newton’s law says cooling rate is proportional to:','["the object’s absolute temperature","the temperature difference from surroundings","the square of elapsed time","the object’s mass only"]',1,'Newton’s law gives a cooling rate proportional to T−Ts for modest temperature differences.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-ideal-gas-equation-01','physics','thermodynamics','Kinetic theory','Ideal gas equation','Which equation describes n moles of an ideal gas?','["PV=nRT","P=nR/VT","PV=RT/n","PVT=nR"]',0,'The ideal-gas equation of state is PV=nRT.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-degrees-freedom-01','physics','thermodynamics','Kinetic theory','Degrees of freedom','A monatomic ideal-gas molecule has how many translational degrees of freedom?','["1","2","3","5"]',2,'It can translate independently along the three spatial axes.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-equipartition-01','physics','thermodynamics','Kinetic theory','Equipartition','At temperature T, the mean energy associated with each quadratic degree of freedom is:','["kT","kT/2","3kT/2","2kT"]',1,'The equipartition theorem assigns kT/2 per quadratic degree of freedom.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-mean-free-path-01','physics','thermodynamics','Kinetic theory','Mean free path','At fixed temperature, increasing gas pressure generally makes molecular mean free path:','["increase","decrease","remain constant","become infinite"]',1,'Higher pressure increases number density and collision frequency, reducing mean free path.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-molecular-speeds-01','physics','thermodynamics','Kinetic theory','Molecular speeds','The rms speed of ideal-gas molecules of molar mass M is:','["√(RT/M)","√(2RT/M)","√(3RT/M)","3RT/M"]',2,'Kinetic theory gives vrms=√(3RT/M).','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-state-variables-01','physics','thermodynamics','Thermodynamic processes','State variables','Which pair consists entirely of thermodynamic state variables?','["heat and work","pressure and volume","work and time","heat and path length"]',1,'Pressure and volume characterize equilibrium states; heat and work depend on the process path.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-first-law-01','physics','thermodynamics','Thermodynamic processes','First law','Using W as work done by the system, the first law of thermodynamics is:','["Q=ΔU+W","Q=ΔU−W","W=Q+ΔU","ΔU=Q+W"]',0,'Energy conservation gives heat supplied Q equal to internal-energy increase plus work done by the system.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('physics-isothermal-adiabatic-01','physics','thermodynamics','Thermodynamic processes','Isothermal and adiabatic processes','Which statement is correct for an ideal gas?','["In an isothermal process ΔU=0; in an adiabatic process Q=0","In both processes Q=0","In both processes ΔU=0","In an isothermal process W=0"]',0,'Ideal-gas internal energy depends only on temperature, while adiabatic means no heat exchange.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Physics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
